playbook investigation y lanza un subagente que lea README.md. No cambies nada.\n\n## Lo que manda el motor sobre pstack\n# poteto-mode dentro de un encargo del motor\n\nEsta página manda sobre `pstack/skills/poteto-mode` (y sus playbooks) donde chocan. Lo que no\nnombra aquí sigue como dice poteto-mode. `<pstack>` es la carpeta `pstack/` de la conf compartida,\nen la ruta absoluta que da el encargo. Cada skill es `<pstack>/skills/<nombre>/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Quién eres\n\nEres un agente de un encargo del motor: una rama, un brief con filas y un `Acepta` por fila. Nadie\nlee tu pantalla. El plan es la autorización de todo lo que el brief pide.\n\n## Lo que cambia\n\n1. **Nunca abres, marcas listo ni mergeas un PR.** Donde un playbook dice \"abre el PR\" (Opening a\n   PR, Autopilot, Shipping), tu equivalente es: un commit por fila con el id de la fila al inicio\n   del mensaje y `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/<tu rama>`. Nada de `gh pr create`, `gh pr\n   ready`, `gh pr merge`, ni su API. Lo demás de Opening a PR sí aplica: `deslop` antes del commit y\n   `no-comments` antes de revisión.\n2. **Babysit y Shipping no aplican.** No vigilas CI ni PRs, no esperas bots, no verificas pilas ni\n   las aterrizas. Lo hace el motor y el revisor.\n3. **No pausas ni preguntas.** Nadie contesta. \"Always pause\", `AskQuestion`, `AskUserQuestion`,\n   Pause safely y todo \"espera al operador\" no aplican. Si una decisión de producto no es tuya,\n   aplica el default…[3784 caracteres más]"}]}}, {"type": "user", "uuid": "66cb2d95-da10-49ac-b6c4-7636ac75b02b", "session_id": "b6d1911d-f403-4826-be1f-af338d17bf59", "parent_tool_use_id": null, "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "call_ebf4a629c2b540b88aa3ba3d", "is_error": false, "content": "---\nname: pstack motor measurement runs\ndescription: The user runs \"mide-pstack\" motor harnesses that grade CLI agents (qwen, claude, codex) against a fixed copy of the pstack skill stack.\ntype: user\ncategory: basic_information\nkeywords:\n  - \"pstack motor\"\n  - \"mide-pstack measurement run\"\n  - \"CLI agent harness\"\n  - \"poteto-mode skill stack\"\n  - \"brief rows and Acepta\"\n  - \"read-only measurement row\"\nusage_scenarios:\n  - \"A brief.md from the motor arrives\"\n  - \"Judging what evidence a run must leave\"\n  - \"Explaining how agent runs get graded\"\n---\n\nThe user builds and runs a measurement harness called `mide-pstack` (the motor). Each run hands the agent a `brief.md`, a fixed copy of the shared `pstack/` config, a branch, brief rows with an `Acepta` line each, and a per-CLI map at `pstack-motor/<cli>.md`.\n\nThe motor grades the tool-call log, not the agent's prose. Something only written down does not count; the action has to appear as a real tool call. The motor itself runs each `Acepta`, and owns CI, PR review, and deploys.\n\nWhat the agent delivers is the branch tip, the SHA, and the `{\"sha\": ..., \"resumen\": ...}` JSON at `$MOTOR_RESULT`.\n\nSome rows are pure measurement rows: they say \"no cambies nada\" and only check the tool-call log for the shape of the run (skill loaded before action N, playbook opened, subagent launched with the absolute skill path in its prompt). Such a row has no diff to review and no commit to make.\n\nNot every run gets a real delivery channel. The work …[261 caracteres más]"}]}}, {"type": "user", "uuid": "8c24e361-4e5f-410b-953e-411a69d017b8", "session_id": "b6d1911d-f403-4826-be1f-af338d17bf59", "parent_tool_use_id": null, "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "call_f51d39c48c78454a86806591", "is_error": false, "content": "---\nname: loading skills and subagents in Qwen Code\ndescription: Confirmed Qwen Code workarounds - no skill or agent CLI flag, the subagent tool is deferred behind tool_search and takes no model parameter, no todo-list tool, and background subagents never report back in single-turn runs.\ntype: user\ncategory: tool_experience\nkeywords:\n  - \"Qwen Code skill loading\"\n  - \"deferred agent tool tool_search\"\n  - \"Explore read-only subagent\"\n  - \"foreground subagent single turn\"\n  - \"missing todo-list tool\"\n  - \"agent tool has no model parameter\"\nusage_scenarios:\n  - \"A brief says to load a pstack skill\"\n  - \"Delegating a read-only investigation step\"\n  - \"A pstack skill names a model per role\"\n---\n\nConfirmed while running motor briefs in Qwen Code 0.25.x on Windows.\n\nSkills have no CLI flag and no skill-loading tool. Load a pstack skill by reading its `SKILL.md` at an absolute path. The `skill` tool only reaches bundled Qwen Code skills, never pstack ones. `agent-delegation` is bundled, and it is the one the `agent` tool tells you to load before writing a delegation prompt.\n\nThe subagent tool is named `agent` but is deferred, so it is not callable directly. Review its schema with `tool_search` on `select:agent`, then launch it with `tool_call`. Its real parameters are `description`, `prompt`, `subagent_type`, and `run_in_background`. It takes no `model`, so the per-role model lines a pstack skill prescribes cannot be honored. Omit `model`, take the skill's `auto` or `inherit-parent` …[604 caracteres más]"}]}}, {"type": "user", "uuid": "d61f8348-a953-45be-954b-aba0ad3bf5d8", "session_id": "b6d1911d-f403-4826-be1f-af338d17bf59", "parent_tool_use_id": null, "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "call_71e5d281f9de404f8bfd4b14", "is_error": false, "content": "---\nname: motor runs are non-interactive and open no PRs\ndescription: In motor/brief runs never pause or ask, never open or merge a PR, and never deploy; commit per row, push the branch, and keep going.\ntype: feedback\ncategory: practice_standard\nkeywords:\n  - \"no pausing or questions\"\n  - \"no gh pr create\"\n  - \"commit per brief row\"\n  - \"smallest default in resumen\"\n  - \"motor owns CI and deploys\"\nusage_scenarios:\n  - \"Executing a brief.md from the motor\"\n  - \"Deciding whether to ask the user mid-run\"\n  - \"A playbook step says to open a PR\"\n---\n\nIn a motor run, do not pause and do not ask. Apply the smallest default, record it in `resumen`, and continue. If only a person can proceed (login, 2FA, captcha, payment), say so in `resumen` and hand over what is done.\n\nNever open, mark ready, or merge a PR. Where a playbook says \"open the PR\", make one commit per brief row with the row id at the start of the message and `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/<branch>`. No `gh pr create`, `gh pr ready`, `gh pr merge`, and no PR API calls.\n\nSkip babysitting and shipping: no CI or PR polling, no stack verification, no landing. Do not deploy, restart services, or touch production. A skipped playbook step stays in the list with a one-line `skip: <reason>` rather than disappearing.\n\n**Why:** nobody answers during the run, and the motor plus its reviewer already own CI, PRs, and deploys.\n\n**How to apply:** any session started from a motor `brief.md` with rows and `Acepta` lines.\n"}]}}, {"type": "assistant", "uuid": "b7b35cfb-b5de-4d39-abbe-cd7023e627a5", "session_id": "b6d1911d-f403-4826-be1f-af338d17bf59", "parent_tool_use_id": null, "message": {"id": "b7b35cfb-b5de-4d39-abbe-cd7023e627a5", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": "qwen3.8-max", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Let me read the motor.md and qwen.md files, then load poteto-mode SKILL.md.\n\nThe brief says: load poteto-mode before action number 6. My actions so far: 4 read_file calls in parallel (actions 1-4 presumably). Let me be careful and load poteto-mode SKILL.md now as the next action.\n\nActually let me read motor.md and qwen.md as instructed, plus poteto-mode SKILL.md in parallel. But the constraint is \"load the skill poteto-mode before your action number 6\". Let me count: the first message had 4 read_file calls = actions 1-4. So actions 5, 6 remain before the deadline. Loading poteto-mode must happen before action 6